get ceiling when discussing how far a face or physique could be improved. They do not change appearance themselves."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["Tera Chad and God tier are slang terms in looksmaxxing culture for levels of attractiveness above Giga Chad, which in turn sits above Chad. The prefix escalation follows metric units, so Tera denotes a further step up [1].","The terms appear in threads that compare men and women, such as a mog battle between a 'Tera Chad' and a 'Tera Stacy', where members argue over whether a pictured person qualifies and whether a photo is edited or a meme [1]. Other threads nominate named people as a Tera Chad [2][3].","'God tier' is used more loosely as a superlative applied to a skin result, a masseter, a physique or a hair product, so it can describe an outcome in a feature as well as a tier of overall looks [4]. No formal scale defines the tiers."],"infobox":[["Type","Community slang / rating tier"],["Position","Above Giga Chad on informal scales"],["Female counterpart","Tera Stacy [1]"],["Formal definition","None"]],"sections":[{"h":"Usage","paras":["In a mog battle thread, one member points out that the 'Tera Chad' body shown comes from a meme and is not the pictured man's real body, while another says a 'Tera Stacy' does not meet the standard despite makeup that adds definition [1]. Threads also nominate individuals as 'legit Tera Chad' or as a Tera Chad with a prettyboy look [2][3]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"God tier as a superlative","paras":["The phrase attaches to many topics: a post about skin after stopping tretinoin describes reaching 'god tier skin' [4], and other threads title routines or features god tier, which stacks the word on products and results rather than people."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[],"refs":[{"title":"Mog Battle Tera Chad vs Tera Stacy","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/tera-chad-vs-tera-stacy.604427/","source":"looksma